From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claudio Saavedra <csaavedra@igalia.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 23:13:23 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] [GLib] AcceleratedSurface destroyed on the main thread with
 its release-unused-buffers timer still active
 https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=327729

Reviewed by NOBODY (OOPS!).

AcceleratedSurface owns a RunLoop::Timer on the compositing run loop, armed
as a 10 second one-shot when the view is hidden. ThreadedCompositor's
invalidate() tore it down by dispatching a lambda to that run loop, holding
a Ref to the surface. The compositor's WorkQueue is destroyed right after
and stops the run loop, and RunLoop::runGLibMainLoop() exits as soon as the
stop flag is set, so when the stop lands between the thread finishing the
preceding dispatchSync and re-checking the flag, the lambda never runs.
Functions dispatched through the WorkQueue hold a reference to it and cannot
be dropped this way; functions handed straight to its RunLoop can. The
lambda is destroyed together with the RunLoop's queue, its Ref was the last
one, and the surface is destroyed on the main run loop with the timer still
active.

Since 316457@main, destroying an active RunLoop::Timer off its run loop's
thread asserts. Builds without assertions are unaffected: by then the
compositing thread has exited, so nothing races with the destructor, and
GLib detaches a context's remaining sources when the context is finalized,
so the g_source_destroy() in ~TimerBase is harmless. On the GLib bots and
EWS, which run with assertions, the inspector tests hide and close the
inspector view within the timer's window: in forced runs of the inspector
suites on GTK and WPE the assertion fired in about one run in fifteen,
nearly always in the inspector frontend's web process as it closes, which
WebKitTestRunner does not attribute to the test, and once in the page's own
process.

Call willDestroyCompositingRunLoop() from a dispatchSync on the work queue
instead, while the compositing run loop is still guaranteed to be running,
and let it destroy the timer directly. The frame-complete handler and the
message receiver are now cleared on the thread that uses them, and the
pending visibility lambda already tolerates a destroyed timer.

* Source/WebKit/WebProcess/WebPage/CoordinatedGraphics/AcceleratedSurface.cpp:
(WebKit::AcceleratedSurface::willDestroyCompositingRunLoop):
* Source/WebKit/WebProcess/WebPage/CoordinatedGraphics/ThreadedCompositor.cpp:
(WebKit::ThreadedCompositor::invalidate):
---
Downstream copy of the upstream fix under review: https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/pull/77182
pinned at commit 1585ffd432979fa2aff7af0b4694129cc2ed08b9, cherry-picked onto the
revision the recipe builds. Replace with the landed commit, or drop when the recipe
moves past it.

 .../CoordinatedGraphics/AcceleratedSurface.cpp       | 12 +++++-------
 .../CoordinatedGraphics/ThreadedCompositor.cpp       |  4 +++-
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/WebPage/CoordinatedGraphics/AcceleratedSurface.cpp b/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/WebPage/CoordinatedGraphics/AcceleratedSurface.cpp
index 8177756a0e14..c18a6374ab38 100644
--- a/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/WebPage/CoordinatedGraphics/AcceleratedSurface.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/WebPage/CoordinatedGraphics/AcceleratedSurface.cpp
@@ -1036,13 +1036,11 @@ void AcceleratedSurface::willDestroyCompositingRunLoop()
         return;
 #endif
 
-    // m_releaseUnusedBuffersTimer is owned by the compositing run loop and its destructor stops it, so
-    // destroy it on that run loop's thread rather than here on the main thread.
-    if (RefPtr compositingRunLoop = std::exchange(m_compositingRunLoop, nullptr)) {
-        compositingRunLoop->dispatch([protectedThis = Ref { *this }] {
-            protectedThis->m_releaseUnusedBuffersTimer = nullptr;
-        });
-    }
+    // Runs on the compositing run loop, which owns m_releaseUnusedBuffersTimer and must be the
+    // thread that destroys it.
+    if (RefPtr compositingRunLoop = std::exchange(m_compositingRunLoop, nullptr))
+        assertIsCurrent(*compositingRunLoop);
+    m_releaseUnusedBuffersTimer = nullptr;
 #if PLATFORM(GTK) || ENABLE(WPE_PLATFORM)
     WebProcess::singleton().parentProcessConnection()->removeMessageReceiver(Messages::AcceleratedSurface::messageReceiverName(), m_id);
 #endif
diff --git a/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/WebPage/CoordinatedGraphics/ThreadedCompositor.cpp b/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/WebPage/CoordinatedGraphics/ThreadedCompositor.cpp
index c238029ad9c9..fef28906ddf2 100644
--- a/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/WebPage/CoordinatedGraphics/ThreadedCompositor.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/WebPage/CoordinatedGraphics/ThreadedCompositor.cpp
@@ -180,7 +180,9 @@ void ThreadedCompositor::invalidate()
     });
     m_sceneState = nullptr;
     m_layerTreeHost = nullptr;
-    m_surface->willDestroyCompositingRunLoop();
+    m_workQueue->dispatchSync([this] {
+        m_surface->willDestroyCompositingRunLoop();
+    });
     m_surface = nullptr;
 }
 
